Koki Recipe

Ingredients:

1kg black-eyed peas

250ml red palm oil

2 seasoning cubes

Salt to taste

Fresh pepper to taste

Banana leaves for wrapping

Water as needed

Preparation:

Wash the black-eyed peas and soak them in water for about 2 hours.

Remove the skins by rubbing the peas between your hands and washing them repeatedly until most of the skins are removed.

Grind the peeled peas into a smooth paste.

Pour the palm oil into a bowl and stir until it becomes lighter in colour.

Add the palm oil to the ground peas. Add salt, seasoning cubes, and pepper. Mix thoroughly, adding a little water if necessary to achieve a thick, smooth mixture.

Wash the banana leaves and soften them over low heat to make them flexible.

Scoop the mixture into the banana leaves and wrap securely.

Arrange the wrapped koki in a pot lined with banana leaves. Add water to the pot, cover, and steam for about 1½ to 2 hours. Check the water occasionally and add more hot water if needed.

Remove from the pot when firm and fully cooked.

Serve hot with boiled ripe plantains, cocoyam, or cassava.
